And `ng` is only available in a dev build but not on prod. I found the issue you referred to during my initial research and it seems unrelated to me, as it apparently only happens while running a dev build. But we faced our issue on production, which increases criticality and urge to find a solution.

@alan-agius4 , build is still done using regular CLI builder, at least this is what works under the hood of `@angular-builders/custom-webpack` builder, we use for slightly adapting the build via custom webpack config, but in a non-impacting way wrt. the server build respectively totally unrelated to any issues with fetching data (what is the actual issue). So please don't take the fact of using a custom builder (not supported by Angular team) as a reason for current issue.

